# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs the dashboard's auth cookies. Generate a fresh one per environment:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Changing it logs everyone out. Never commit the real value.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Selects the adapter in payload.config.ts: a postgres:// value uses Postgres,
# unset uses the local SQLite file, which is what local development wants.
# SQLite CANNOT be used on Vercel.
#
# DATABASE_URL and POSTGRES_URL are read as fallbacks, in that order, because
# those are the names Vercel's Postgres integrations inject for you — so
# attaching a database in the Vercel dashboard needs nothing set by hand here.
# Set DATABASE_URI only to override that.
#
# Anything that is neither postgres:// nor file:/libsql: throws on startup
# rather than quietly falling back to SQLite. Note that Neon's Data API URL
# (https://…apirest…/rest/v1) is NOT a connection string.
# See "Going to production" in CMS.md.
# DATABASE_URI=postgres://user:password@host-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require

# ── Uploads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel injects this once a Blob store is attached to the project. Unset,
# the storage plugin turns itself off and uploads stay in public/media, which
# is correct locally and broken on a serverless host.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ── Email (Zend) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Outbound email — the submission alert to staff and password resets — goes
# through the Zend API (tryzend.com). All unset: every email is written to the
# server console instead, which is what local development wants. Setting only
# one of the first two throws at boot rather than silently never sending.
# See "Email delivery" in CMS.md for the dashboard setup (domain verification,
# API key scope).
# ZEND_API_KEY=
# The from address; its domain must be verified in Zend (Email → Domains).
# ZEND_FROM_EMAIL=info@blackinrehab.com
# Optional display name; defaults to "Black in Rehab".
# ZEND_FROM_NAME="Black in Rehab"

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The site's public URL, used for CORS and absolute links in emails.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://blackinrehab.org

# ── Ticketing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Checkout link for The Connection Table™: Indianapolis (/connection-table/
# indianapolis). Every "reserve my seat" button on that page points here.
#
# Unset, the buttons drop the visitor at the ticket panel, which says when
# sales open instead of going nowhere — so the page is safe to publish before
# the link exists. It is read at build time, so changing it needs a redeploy.
#
# The link must collect, on top of Stripe's own name and email:
#   1. Meal Selection   dropdown, REQUIRED, one option per entrée
#   2. Profession       dropdown, REQUIRED — SLP / SLPA / Student
#   3. Allergies        text, optional
# Cap it at the seat count and keep quantity at one per checkout, so each
# ticket carries its own meal answer in the payments export.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONNECTION_TABLE_URL=https://buy.stripe.com/...
